<title>NORWAY: NORDIC SKIING-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIPS MEDALS TABLE.</title>
<headline>NORDIC SKIING-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIPS MEDALS TABLE.</headline>
<dateline>TRONDHEIM, Norway 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Medals table at the</p>
<p>Nordic skiing world championships after six days on Wednesday</p>
<p>(tabulated under gold, silver, bronze):</p>
<p> 1. Russia		     4	    2	    3</p>
<p> 2. Norway		     3	    2	    1</p>
<p> 3. Finland		    1	    2	    1</p>
<p> 4. Japan			1	    1	    0</p>
<p> 5. Italy			0	    3	    0</p>
<p> 6. Austria		    0	    0	    2</p>
<p> 7 equal. Czech Republic   0	    0	    1</p>
<p> 7 equal. France	     0	    0	    1</p>
<p>Note: this table takes count of Russian Lyubov Yegorova's</p>
<p>disqualification for doping.</p>
</text>
